IBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.7.rc2.mono.official [3df26a02c]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.rc2.mono - Windows 10 (build 17134) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1070 (NVIDIA; 31.0.15.3141) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-7700 CPU @ 3.60GHz (8 threads) - 23.92 GiB memory - WASAPI (96000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nThis is a really strange one.\nThe new search bar feature https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114236 does not work sometimes.\n\nThe BonesAttachment bone_name search poup does not work when using it with .blend imported models. \nWhile it works normally for .glb imported models.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e20c5a05-9901-4b65-be8c-e2f958e3e6e9\n\nAnd I'm not sure if this is a limitation or a bug. But it also does not seems to be working with exported enums either:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5c8e6943-71ba-450c-baab-c1e9092c7ce2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Import a model from **.blend asset** inside the scene\n- Enable editable children\n- Add a bone attachment or bone modifier inside the skeleton 3d\n- Select a bone \n\nResult: No search popup for the bone selection\nExpected: Search bar for the bone selection\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[search popupmenu MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28918156/search.popupmenu.MRP.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"GustJc","id":3084189,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwODQxODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3084189?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc","html_url":"https://github.com/GustJc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GustJc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/